# Jimmy's ruling, 12 November: `forall`. Only a signature's `forall` puts its variables
# in scope in the body. `Swap`'s signature has no `forall`, so its `b` is not in scope in
# the body, and `Make<<b>>` names nothing: `unknown-name`. With `Swap: forall a b. fn
# ((a, b)) -> ((b, a))` the program checks (conformance/forall-three-jobs).
# Expected diagnostic derived by hand. Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting
# branch; subject to change.
Make: fn b, a -> ((b, a))
fn Make second, first = ((second, first))

Swap: fn ((a, b)) -> ((b, a))
fn Swap pair = match pair:
    ((first, second)): Make<<b>> second, first
